# Line endings: LF everywhere, including in the working tree.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout writes CRLF, and two things that read
# source line by line quietly broke on it while staying green in CI:
#
#   - scripts/check-emoji.mjs stripped comments with a regex ending in
#     `$`, which JavaScript will not match before a carriage return -- so
#     every emoji merely written *about* in a comment was reported.
#   - Vitest's shebang handling expects `#!...\n`. With `\r\n` the line
#     survived into the parser, and importing a check script from a test
#     failed the whole suite with "Invalid or unexpected token".
#
# CI runs on Linux and never saw either.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries Git must not touch.
*.png binary
*.webp binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
